{{Quote|&hellip;if you've never seen a Fledgling Mythrol evacuate their thorax, you're a lucky guy, trust me.|A Mythrol, to Din Djarin|<ref name="Chapter 1" />}}
The '''Mythrol''' were a [[Sentience|sentient]] [[humanoid]] [[species]] with [[Amphibian|amphibious]] traits.

==Biology and appearance==
The Mythrol had [[Amphibian|amphibious]] traits such as gills and fins on their heads. They had thoraxes which had to be "evacuated" and could molt. Young Mythrol could produce a sweet musk.<ref name="Chapter 1" /> After molting, their faces would become barbed.<ref name="TROS VD" /> Mythrol at a younger age were referred to as "fledglings."<ref name="Chapter 1" />

They could even live for a few hundred years.<ref name="Chapter 12" />

==Mythrol in the galaxy==
In [[200 BBY]],<ref name="VowDate">''[[Star Wars: Timelines]]'' dates ''[[The Vow of Silver Dawn]]'' to [[200 BBY]].</ref> towards the end of the [[High Republic Era]], a [[Unidentified Mythrol|Mythrol]] [[Gender|male]] worked as a [[chef]] for [[President]] [[Jamie Brasson|Jamie Brasen]] at his estate on the [[planet]] of [[Begamor]].<ref name="Silver Dawn">''[[The Vow of Silver Dawn]]''</ref>

By [[9 ABY]],<ref name="Mandalorian-Date">{{MandoDate|12}}</ref> a [[The Fledgling Mythrol|fledgling Mythrol]] was in the employ of [[Magistrate]] [[Greef Karga]] on [[Nevarro]], before he stole from him and fled.<ref name="Chapter 12">{{TheMandalorian|Chapter 12: The Siege}}</ref> Sometime later, he resided on the [[Water|ice]] planet [[Pagodon]] within a [[Boatman's Reach|bar]], where he was harassed by a group of trawlers until the [[Mandalorian]] [[bounty hunter]] [[Din Djarin]] entered. After dealing with the trawlers, Djarin captured the Mythrol and turned him over to the [[Bounty Hunters' Guild]].<ref name="Chapter 1" /> Sometime later, the Mythrol was allowed by Karga to work off his debt to him through three hundred and fifty [[Standard year|years]] of indentured servitude. During that time, he aided Karga, Din Djarin, and [[Marshal]] [[Carasynthia Dune]] in [[Second skirmish on Nevarro|infiltrating and destroying]] a [[Nevarro Imperial base|remnant Imperial base]].<ref name="Chapter 12" />

In [[35 ABY]],<ref name="EpIX-Date">{{FilmDate|IX}}</ref> the post-fledgling Mythrol [[Junn Gobint]] managed [[fuel]] supplies for the [[Resistance]]<ref name="TROS VD" /> during their [[First Order-Resistance War|war]] against the [[First Order]].<ref name="TROS">{{Film|IX}}</ref>

==Behind the scenes==
The Mythrol species first appeared in [[Chapter 1: The Mandalorian|Chapter 1]] of [[Jon Favreau]]'s [[2019]] [[Disney+]] television series ''[[Star Wars: The Mandalorian]]'',<ref name="Chapter 1" /> which aired on [[November 12]], 2019.<ref name="DTCI">{{WebCite|url=https://lumiere-a.akamaihd.net/v1/documents/the_mandalorian_project_one-sheet_10_ec1e005f.pdf|text=The Mandalorian Media Kit|work=[https://dtcimedia.disney.com Disney Direct-to-Consumer & International]|archivedate=20230315011507}}</ref> While writing the [[Star Wars: The Rise of Skywalker: The Visual Dictionary|visual dictionary]] for the 2019 film [[Star Wars: Episode IX The Rise of Skywalker|''Star Wars'': Episode IX ''The Rise of Skywalker'']], [[Lucasfilm Story Group]] member [[Pablo Hidalgo]] made a connection between ''The Mandalorian''{{'s}} Mythrol and the similar looking background alien Junn Gobint in Episode IX. Taking the television character's background as a "fledgling" into account, Hidalgo established in the dictionary that the independently designed aliens belonged to the same species.<ref name="TROS VD" /><ref name="Szostak Twitter">{{Twitter|PhilSzostak|status/1306012409031733254|[[Phil Szostak]]|quote=Correct me if I'm wrong, but I believe they were developed by separate teams independently of each other, with @pablohidalgo making the connection when he wrote The TROS Visual Dictionary. Since the Mando Mythrol had more backstory, that one drove the narrative.|archiveurl=https://archive.is/FdfQi}}</ref>

